# Makes one value safe for a single tab separated line. The one place that
# does this, so the reader has exactly one thing to mirror.
#
# LIMIT, named on purpose: the backslash itself is NOT escaped. A value that
# already carried the two characters backslash and n comes back as a real
# line break. Escaping the escape needs a scanner, and no $desc has yet
# earned one. If one ever does, this method is the only thing to change.

Calculate text as pText
Calculate text as replaceall(text,kCr,'\n')
Calculate text as replaceall(text,kLf,'\n')
Calculate text as replaceall(text,kTab,'\t')
Quit method text